    "success_criteria": {
      "criteria": [
        "AgentCostTelemetryAdapter and CodexBudgetAdapter constructed without timeoutMs use 180_000 ms, exported as one shared constant (DEFAULT_AGENT_COST_TIMEOUT_MS) that a test asserts equals 180_000 and that both adapters expose as their effective timeout.",
        "When agent-cost is killed by the adapter's timeout, the thrown error's message contains \"timed out after <timeoutMs> ms\" and the kill signal, asserted by a test that runs a fake agent-cost that sleeps longer than a 200 ms timeout and that fails against the pre-change code (which only reports \"Command failed\").",
        "A non-timeout failure (agent-cost exits non-zero, or the binary does not exist) still throws the existing \"agent-cost measure failed (bin=...)\" / \"agent-cost report failed (bin=...)\" message with the original error text appended, and that message does not claim a timeout.",
        "lane calibrate, lane emit-metrics, lane next and lane usage-import each accept --agent-cost-timeout-ms <n>, and the value reaches the adapter through main.ts's real commander definitions, asserted by a subprocess test per command that runs a sleeping fake agent-cost with --agent-cost-timeout-ms 200 and observes the \"timed out after 200 ms\" failure.",
        "--agent-cost-timeout-ms rejects 0, a negative number, a non-integer and a non-numeric string with a non-zero exit and a usage error naming the flag, before agent-cost is spawned; the accepted range is 1..3_600_000 inclusive.",
        "On the machine that reproduced issue #42, `lane calibrate I-2026-09-17-dd-report-cwd-baseline-append --session-id 30cf8740-bc2f-4f1d-be00-f866aabd5f43` (deterministic-discipline cwd, default timeout) exits 0 and writes a scope:\"lane\" cost_ledger entry for that lane.",
        "CHANGELOG.md gains an entry for the new flag, the new default and the timeout message, and README.md's agent-cost paragraph documents --agent-cost-timeout-ms next to --agent-cost-bin."
      ],
      "recorded_at": "2026-09-17T09:16:04.160Z"
    }
